  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Crossing figure eights from two queues",
  "description": "Set up two circles of four cones each in one half of the rink, one on each side. Split the players into two queues by the boards a little in front of the centre line. The first player in each queue starts at the same time, skates diagonally across so the paths cross in the middle, skates a full lap round the circle on the opposite side and joins the back of the other queue. The next pair go on the coach's signal or when the first pair have left the circle.\n\nSkate the laps both ways: switch starting sides after a few rounds so the turns are made both to the right and to the left. Progressions: with a ball, higher tempo, or crossovers round the circle. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up at the crossing – it is up to you not to collide."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Lean into the turn and push your outside shoulder forward round the circle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Low skating position with the stick on the ice."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Full speed out of the circle, not just into it."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
